git init - initialize git in the current directory(cd) / create repo locally
git add - used to track the file by git (send the file in staging area)
git diff - tells the difference b/w this and previous version
git rm - remove the file from tracking
git commit - to commit the code (in the staging area)
git log - show the histroy of commits
git show :id - shows the changes made on the commit id
git blame :file - shows the log of every line
git status - local changes
git reset --hard :commit_id - to revert back changes (deltes the previous commit)
git revert :commit_id - to revert the particular code

GITHUB

git rmeote add :nickname_name :link - connect to github
git push -u :nickname :branch - push to branch
git push -f - used to push forcefully (when the local and server head are different)

